# BGWEAPON - weapon slots, ammo and ammo costs for Begotten.
#
# The 8 slots each hold one weapon with a primary and a secondary (alt) fire
# mode.  Every mode is one of the engine's 16 weapon entries:
#
#   fist  pistol  shotgun  chaingun  missile  plasma  bfg  chainsaw  supershotgun
#   dualpistols  chainfire  tornado  arclightning  snap  hellfire  spare
#
# (numbers 0-15 work too).  In the game these are:
#   knife (fist), pistol (the strong single shot), revolver (dualpistols, the weaker piercing shot), rifle (shotgun), scattergun
#   (supershotgun), machinegun (chaingun), chaingun (chainfire), fireball (missile),
#   devil's breath (plasma), tornado, arc lightning, snap, thunderclap (bfg),
#   hellfire, chainsaw.
#
# Lines (anything after # or // is a comment):
#
#   slot <1-8> primary <weapon> alt <weapon|none>
#   ammo <type> max <n> clip <n>       type: bullets shells belts fire tempest spirit hellfire
#       max = most the player can carry (a backpack doubles it);
#       clip = what a small pickup gives (a big one gives 5x).
#   mode <weapon> ammo <type|none> use <n>
#       which ammo the mode uses and how much one shot costs.
#
# Later lines (and BGWEAPON lumps in your own WAD) override earlier ones.
# DEHACKED "Ammo per shot" and "Ammo type" of weapons are overridden by this lump.

slot 1 primary fist       alt chainsaw
slot 2 primary pistol     alt dualpistols
slot 3 primary shotgun    alt supershotgun
slot 4 primary chaingun   alt chainfire
slot 5 primary plasma     alt missile
slot 6 primary tornado    alt arclightning
slot 7 primary snap       alt bfg
slot 8 primary hellfire   alt none
ammo bullets  max 200 clip 20
ammo shells   max 60  clip 6
ammo belts    max 300 clip 30
ammo fire     max 200 clip 20
ammo tempest  max 200 clip 20
ammo spirit   max 100 clip 10
ammo hellfire max 50  clip 5
mode fist         ammo none
mode chainsaw     ammo none
mode pistol       ammo bullets  use 1
mode dualpistols  ammo bullets  use 1

# Revolver primary: ONE bullet, damage = (1..mod) x damage, stopped by the first thing it hits.
# The pistol troopers (3004) fire with the same numbers (their foedamage % still applies).
# spread is in tenths of a degree.
pistolshot damage 10 mod 3 spread 40

# Revolver secondary: ONE bullet, damage = (1..mod) x damage, that goes through up to `hits` monsters;
# every monster after the first takes `falloff` percent of what the one before it took.
# spread is in tenths of a degree.  (Its recovery time is in the weapon states: about 40 tics.)
pierce damage 6 mod 3 hits 5 falloff 85 spread 0

mode shotgun      ammo shells   use 1
mode supershotgun ammo shells   use 4
mode chaingun     ammo belts    use 1
mode chainfire    ammo belts    use 1
mode missile      ammo fire     use 4
mode plasma       ammo fire     use 1
mode tornado      ammo tempest  use 5
mode arclightning ammo tempest  use 4
mode snap         ammo spirit   use 5
mode bfg          ammo spirit   use 25
mode hellfire     ammo hellfire use 1
mode spare        ammo none     use 0
